§§ `Section 59.1(7) -- adjustment factor for a contributor 70 or older`

-- src:1999 | Adjustment factor for contributors — 70 years of age or older
-- src:2000 | (7) For the purposes of the calculations under subsections (1.1), (3) and (5), if the contributor is 70 years of age or older, the adjustment factor referred to in E in each of those subsections is that of a contributor who is 70 years of age.
@ref Act s 59.1(7) (src:2000)
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the year in which the post-retirement benefit commences to be payable` IS A DATE
      `the adjustment factor for the contributor's age on that day` IS A NUMBER
      `the adjustment factor of a contributor who is 70 years of age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 59.1(7) — the adjustment factor E` `date of birth` `the first day of the year in which the post-retirement benefit commences to be payable` `the adjustment factor for the contributor's age on that day` `the adjustment factor of a contributor who is 70 years of age` MEANS
    -- "if the contributor is 70 years of age or older": tested on 1 January of the year of commencement, the day on
    -- which E is "based on the age of the contributor" (NOTES.md, fork register); reaching 70 goes through section 2(2).
    IF `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `date of birth` 70 `the first day of the year in which the post-retirement benefit commences to be payable`
    THEN `the adjustment factor of a contributor who is 70 years of age`
    ELSE `the adjustment factor for the contributor's age on that day`

§§ `Section 59.1(1) -- the aggregate`

-- src:1939 | Amount of post-retirement benefit
-- src:1940 | 59.1 (1) A post-retirement benefit payable to a contributor is a basic monthly amount that is equal to the aggregate of the amounts calculated as provided in subsections (1.1), (3) and (5).
@ref Act s 59.1(1) (src:1940)
GIVEN `the amount calculated as provided in subsection (1.1)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the amount calculated as provided in subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the amount calculated as provided in subsection (5)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 59.1(1) — the basic monthly amount of a post-retirement benefit` `the amount calculated as provided in subsection (1.1)` `the amount calculated as provided in subsection (3)` `the amount calculated as provided in subsection (5)` MEANS
    -- NOTHING if any portion is NOTHING: the text then gives no aggregate.
    CONSIDER `the amount calculated as provided in subsection (1.1)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST base THEN
        CONSIDER `the amount calculated as provided in subsection (3)`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST firstAdditional THEN
            CONSIDER `the amount calculated as provided in subsection (5)`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST secondAdditional THEN JUST (base PLUS firstAdditional PLUS secondAdditional)

§ `Section 59.2 -- post-retirement disability benefit`

-- src:2004 | 59.2 A post-retirement disability benefit payable to a contributor is a basic monthly amount that is
-- src:2005 | (a) in the case of a benefit payable for a month in the year 2019, an amount calculated by multiplying
-- src:2006 | (i) $485.20
-- src:2007 | by
-- src:2008 | (ii) the ratio that the Pension Index for 2019 bears to the Pension Index for 2018; and
-- src:2009 | (b) in the case of a benefit payable for a month in the year 2020 or any subsequent year, an amount calculated by multiplying
-- src:2010 | (i) the amount of the benefit that would have been payable for a month in the year preceding that year
-- src:2011 | by
-- src:2012 | (ii) the ratio that the Pension Index for the year in which the benefit is payable bears to the Pension Index for the year preceding that year.
@ref Act s 59.2 (src:2004-2012)
GIVEN `the year for which the benefit is payable` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 59.2 — the basic monthly amount of a post-retirement disability benefit` `the year for which the benefit is payable` `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the year for which the benefit is payable` EQUALS 2019
            THEN `cp4 an amount that may be missing times a ratio that may be missing` (JUST 485.20) (`cp4 the ratio of the Pension Index for a year to the Pension Index for the year before` 2019 `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986`)
        IF `the year for which the benefit is payable` AT LEAST 2020
            THEN `cp4 an amount that may be missing times a ratio that may be missing` (`s 59.2 — the basic monthly amount of a post-retirement disability benefit` (`the year for which the benefit is payable` MINUS 1) `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986`) (`cp4 the ratio of the Pension Index for a year to the Pension Index for the year before` `the year for which the benefit is payable` `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
